--TEST--
`Core\Http\Client::openSocket` speaks `ws` and `wss` and no other row does, so what a URL is for is written in the row that takes it — `rule:http-server/allow-url-pins-the-address`, `rule:http-server/an-outbound-socket-is-opened-like-an-outbound-call`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// Agreement over the roster: the same question is asked of both halves of the
// class, and each answers with the two schemes it speaks rather than with the
// four the launderer admits. A row that grew its own roster fails here while
// still looking right on its own line.
Core\Test::answerSocket("ws://gateway.example.test/plain", ["over plain ws"]);

// `ws` is allowed as plain `http` is, and there is no downgrade question,
// because a socket follows no redirect.
var $plain = Core\Http\Client::openSocket("ws://gateway.example.test/plain");
echo "plain ", $plain->receive()?->text() ?? "-", "\n";
echo "protocol=", $plain->protocol() ?? "none", "\n";

// The socket row refuses the two a request takes.
try {
    var $https = Core\Http\Client::openSocket("https://gateway.example.test/plain");
} catch (RuntimeError $secure) {
    echo $secure->message, "\n";
}
try {
    var $plainHttp = Core\Http\Client::openSocket("http://gateway.example.test/plain");
} catch (RuntimeError $cleartext) {
    echo $cleartext->message, "\n";
}

// And every request row refuses the two the socket row takes, so a URL
// laundered meaning one thing cannot be spent as the other.
try {
    var $fetched = Core\Http\Client::get("wss://gateway.example.test/plain");
} catch (RuntimeError $fetch) {
    echo $fetch->message, "\n";
}
try {
    var $streamed = Core\Http\Client::stream(Core\Http\Method::Post, "ws://gateway.example.test/plain");
} catch (RuntimeError $streamref) {
    echo $streamref->message, "\n";
}

// The launderer admits all four, so the socket URL gets past the roster and is
// refused for the grant it has not been given instead — what it approves is a
// host and its addresses rather than an intention.
try {
    var $target = Core\Http::allowUrl("wss://gateway.example.test/plain" as tainted string);
} catch (RuntimeError $laundered) {
    echo $laundered->message, "\n";
}

echo "sent=", Core\Arr::count(Core\Test::sentSocket()), "\n";
--EXPECT--
plain over plain ws
protocol=none
Core\Http\Client::openSocket: the scheme must be `ws` or `wss`, and this URL names `https`
Core\Http\Client::openSocket: the scheme must be `ws` or `wss`, and this URL names `http`
Core\Http\Client::get: the scheme must be `http` or `https`, and this URL names `wss`
Core\Http\Client::stream: the scheme must be `http` or `https`, and this URL names `ws`
Core\Http::allowUrl needs the capability `net.connect` for gateway.example.test, which is not granted
help: grant it in nvs.toml under `[capabilities.net]`
sent=0
